WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
<b>CALPIS THEATER</b>

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.060
Subs: English

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.060
S

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.060
<b><i>SILVER ZERO
 SUBS</i></b>

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.060
http://silverzerosubs.blogspot.com/

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:33.800
Original story by Johanna Spyri

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:33.800
<b>Alps no Shoujo Heidi</b>

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.950
Kuchibue ha naze

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.950
<u>Why can a whistle</u>

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.110
<u>be heard from afar?</u>

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.110
Tooku made kikoeru no

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.320
<u>Why is that cloud</u>

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.320
Ano kumo ha naze

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.460
<u>waiting for me?</u>

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.460
Watashi wo matteru no

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.810
<u>Tell me grandfather</u>

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.810
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:50.700
<u>Tell me grandfather</u>

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:50.700
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:59.390
<u>Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm</u>

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:59.390
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.540
To the Alm Mountain

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:35.310
Woah...Woah...

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:41.670
Hello, Heidi. What are you doing here
so early in the morning?

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.990
I'm waiting for my Aunt.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.560
Your Aunt Dete?

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.220
Good morning, Mr. Thomas.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:52.190
Hi! Where are you going so early?

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.600
To Dorfli. And you?

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.800
I'm going to Mayenfeld.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.890
Then, can you give us a ride?

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.200
Yes, of course.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:03.560
Ok Heidi, wrap this shawl around you.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:06.230
There.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.150
It's hot.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:09.880
I know, but this way you won't lose it, right?

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:10.740
There.

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:15.260
On you go...

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.570
I see!

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:36.640
So, are you going to the the Alps,
to leave Heidi with her grandfather?

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.620
I don't want to, but I have no choice.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:44.140
I've found a good job, but I can't take such
a small child. You understand, right?

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.850
<i>Heidi is five years old.</i>

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:01.600
<i>Her mother and father passed
away when she was one.</i>

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.420
<i>Heidi was left alone, but afterwards...</i>

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:07.230
<i>her Aunt Dete brought her up on her own.</i>

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:10.300
<i>However, she was mostly left in the custody of others</i>

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:13.860
<i>and had to lead a lonely life until today.</i>

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:33.610
Woah!

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:03.280
Heidi!

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.820
Heidi, what are you doing?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.150
Do you want to stay behind?

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.430
Well, we're here.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:34.900
Thank you.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.630
Heidi, let's go.

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:43.830
Goodbye, Mr. Thomas.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.260
Take care, Heidi.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:56.620
Poor girl. She is always
going from one place to another.

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:23.360
Come on. Walk faster!

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.560
Heidi, you must hurry up.

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:41.960
Heidi, hurry up.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:09.710
Heidi, are you tired?

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:10.870
I'm hot.

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:12.400
It's just a little further.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:17.230
Look! That's Dorfli,
the village where you were born.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:22.700
The village where I was born?

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:31.630
Listen, it's the church bell.

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.210
Well, let's go.

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:45.970
If it isn't Dete!

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:45.970
Good morning.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.190
Won't you come in?

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.570
I can't. I'm in a hurry.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.270
Oh! If it isn't Dete!

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:55.790
How are you?

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:59.510
I've heard that you were working in the
baths of Bad Ragaz. Are you well?

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:01.010
Yes. I'm fine.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:04.920
So, who is this little girl? Your daughter?

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:07.210
Of course not. It's Heidi.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:08.860
Heidi?

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:12.800
You remember my sister, Adelheid?
This is her child.

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:14.640
Oh! Dete!

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:15.500
Hello!

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:16.550
Who is she?

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.360
She's Heidi. Adelaide's daughter.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:24.370
Oh, this child? Oh, isn't she cute?

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:26.650
And today? You're visiting the grave?

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:30.000
I'm going to take her to Alm-Uncle.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:31.440
Alm-Uncle!

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.920
Why are you going to take her to Alm-Uncle?

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:40.750
I have found a good job in Frankfurt.
And I can't take her with me.

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:43.570
Wait a minute...

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:48.220
Don't scare me like that!

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:49.930
Dete, is that true?

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:51.090
Yes.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:55.730
Listen, you must be kidding.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:59.290
You can't take her to Alm-Uncle.
Don't you think?

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:00.590
That's right.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:03.570
He is an eccentric old man with a
face full of disorderly whiskers.

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:04.680
I agree!

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:05.890
Dete.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.410
I'm in a hurry.
I can not lose more time.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.030
Doing that to such a cute child.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:13.820
Dete does not know what she's doing.

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:20.190
That's crazy.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.810
Why? Alm-Uncle is her Grandfather.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:27.730
But he's not like us. Don't you think?

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:32.500
He never goes to the church. And during
the winter he does not leave the mountain.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.920
He is a terrible man.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:40.620
I'd be afraid of meeting him when I was
alone. I would run away from him.

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:34.980
Dear, what a child!

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:40.410
Oh, I can't tell if it's
snot or sweat in that face.

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:41.760
Here, look at me.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:44.810
Dete!

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:46.130
Is it you, Dete?

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:53.920
Well, that is rather pathetic.
Try putting yourself in Heidi's place.

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:59.410
Not only that, but he's bound to
send you packing home again.

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:30.070
I'm sorry for before.

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:34.370
Snowflake!

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:36.350
Snowflake!

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.940
Its name is Snowflake?

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:49.840
It's yours?

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:54.340
No, it's not.

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:16.640
I'm all right.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:20.920
Wait!

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:26.300
Hey, do all those goats belong to you?

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:27.720
They belong to other people.

00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:40.190
But Dete! You know what kind
of person the old man was!

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.600
What's in the past, it's in the past.

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:44.900
Where is Heidi?

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:46.870
Ah, there she is.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:50.370
Peter will take care of her,
so you don't have to worry.

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:51.960
Heidi is old enough to take care of herself.

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:54.570
She'll get along with the old man somehow.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:59.780
But it's highly unlikely that she'll
get along with someone like Alm-Uncle.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:02.240
I shouldn't say this loudly,

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:04.780
but don't they say that he murdered
someone when he was young?

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:13.330
Why can a whistle

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:13.330
Kuchibue ha naze

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:15.440
be heard from afar?

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:15.440
Tooku made kikoeru no

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:15.100
Wait!

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.730
Why is that cloud

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.730
Ano kumo ha naze

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:19.990
waiting for me?

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:19.990
Watashi wo matteru no

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:21.200
Wait!

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:24.220
Tell me, grandfather

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:24.220
Oshiete ojiisan

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:27.990
Tell me, grandfather

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:27.990
Oshiete ojiisan

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:36.670
Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:36.670
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.890
Why is the mountain snow

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.890
Yuki no yama naze

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:50.170
dyed in rose-color?

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:50.170
Barairo ni somaru no

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:52.670
Where is that wind

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:52.670
Ano kaze ha doko ni

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:54.540
hiding?

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:54.540
Kakureteiru no

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:58.610
Tell me, grandfather

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:58.610
Oshiete ojiisan

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:02.680
Tell me, grandfather

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:02.680
Oshiete ojiisan

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:10.950
Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:10.950
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:30.710
Why do the stars secretly watch

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:30.710
Nemuru toki naze

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:33.020
over me when I'm sleeping?

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:33.020
Hoshi ha sotto miteiru no

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:35.090
Why does it always feel so warm

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:35.090
Wara no naka naze

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:37.370
inside the straw?

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:37.370
Itsumo attakai no

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:39.080
I am Heidi.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:41.680
Tell me, grandfather

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:41.680
Oshiete ojiisan

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.010
My name is Heidi.

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:45.470
Tell me, grandfather

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:45.470
Oshiete ojiisan

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:45.650
Heidi.

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:53.840
Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:53.840
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:47.230
And you?

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:50.920
I... I am Peter.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:52.780
I'm going to the top of the mountain.

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:54.390
The top of the mountain?

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:55.880
To my grandfather's place.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.720
You're going to Alm-Uncle's place?

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:00.150
Uncle?

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:02.980
Everyone in the village calls him that.

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:06.850
That's a weird way to address someone.

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.850
Are you laughing? Aren't you afraid?

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:11.020
Why?

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:13.190
Why, you ask?

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:16.390
Oh well.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.690
Where are you taking the goats?

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:22.740
To the top of the mountains.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:24.370
For what?

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:26.750
To eat good grass.

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:35.680
Look, that goat is mine.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.850
Then, that's your house, Peter?

00:16:39.030 --> 00:16:40.060
That's right.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:43.260
It's late.

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:45.530
Uncle will get mad.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:46.780
I have to go.

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:49.850
<i>Peter is eleven years old.</i>

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:53.060
<i>His late father was also a goatherd.</i>

00:16:53.270 --> 00:16:57.650
<i>During the summer, Peter takes
charge of the goats every day,</i>

00:16:57.650 --> 00:17:00.030
<i>and looks after them by himself.</i>

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:02.160
Right, I've reached my destination.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:06.190
I don't want to be harsh with you, but I
suggest you reconsider the whole idea.

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:06.920
See you.

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:12.960
Aunt!

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:18.540
Heidi, where are your clothes?

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:24.660
Have you lost your senses?
Go quickly and collect your things.

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:27.300
I don't want any clothes.
It's hot.

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.110
What are you saying?

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:31.280
Oh, I know!

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.250
Peter, could you go fetch them?

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:36.810
I'll be late then.

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:39.220
But see, you shall have something nice.

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:42.600
Eh? You'll give me that?

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:45.380
Yes, that's right.
If you go fetch them for me.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.090
I'm going.

00:17:50.490 --> 00:17:51.600
I'm going, too.

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:52.590
- You stay here.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:02.840
Here!

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.500
My! That was fast.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:32.770
Is that, Grandfather's house?

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:11.820
Grandfather, good afternoon.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:18.500
Good afternoon, Grandfather.

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:23.520
So, so, what is the meaning of this?

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:28.930
Good afternoon, Uncle.

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:31.410
This girl is your Granddaughter, Heidi.

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:40.850
You will hardly recognise her, as you have
never seen her since she was a year old.

00:19:44.110 --> 00:19:45.530
Peter!

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:47.160
You're late this morning!

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:49.870
Stop lingering. Hurry and
be off with your goats!

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:51.410
Take my goats, too!

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:54.530
I'm going t...

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:57.020
Heidi, you can't go.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:02.810
So, why have you brought her here?

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:05.530
I want her to remain with you.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:13.450
Uncle, I have done my duty by
her for these four years

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:16.090
and now it is time for you to do yours.

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:20.630
I see, but if you do that

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:23.420
and the child begins to fret and run after you,

00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:25.720
what am I to do with her then?

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:28.150
She's too young.

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:30.560
That's your affair, Uncle.

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:32.870
What you just said was too selfish!

00:20:33.110 --> 00:20:37.000
Selfish? Then I'll go ahead and say this.

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:40.250
When this child was still an
infant, and I already had

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:43.460
enough to do as it was for my mother and myself,

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:47.920
no one in the world told me what
was I to do with this child.

00:20:48.460 --> 00:20:51.300
Now I have to go and look after my own earnings,

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:55.180
and you are the next of kin to the child.

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:58.220
Heidi is your son's child!

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:06.650
If you cannot arrange to keep
her, do with her as you like.

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:09.110
You'll be answerable if anything happens to her.

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:12.780
But of course, you're the type who
won't bother about such things.

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:16.780
Go away!

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:19.050
I've heard enough!

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:22.390
Be off with you this instant, you hear me?!

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:24.830
And don't show your face ever again!

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:35.090
Then Heidi,

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:38.960
do you understand? From now on,
you're going to live here.

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:40.720
Take care of yourself.

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.100
Goodbye, Aunt.

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:21.650
Well, what do you plan to do from now on?

00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:30.630
<i>Grandfather seems to be a very difficult person.</i>

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:35.220
<i>Alone with grandfather in
the Alm Mountain cabin,</i>

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:38.980
<i>what will happen to Heidi now?</i>

00:23:55.620 --> 00:23:59.080
<i>After bidding farewell to Aunt Dete,
Heidi remains on the mountain.</i>

00:23:59.080 --> 00:24:01.960
<i>There she sees and hears
new things everywhere,</i>

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:05.090
<i>which makes her feel very light-hearted.</i>

00:24:05.210 --> 00:24:07.590
<i>But her difficult grandfather</i>

00:24:07.590 --> 00:24:12.130
<i>is still sulking, even after
Aunt Dete has left the mountain.</i>

00:24:12.260 --> 00:24:14.720
<i>Heidi doesn't seem to mind that.</i>

00:24:14.900 --> 00:24:17.560
<i>She makes a bed of straw for herself,</i>

00:24:17.560 --> 00:24:19.640
<i>goes along with Peter and
the baby goat Snowflake outside,</i>

00:24:19.640 --> 00:24:21.940
<i>runs around, and is in real high spirits.</i>

00:24:22.650 --> 00:24:25.470
<i>Next week:
Grandfather's Mountain Cabin</i>

00:24:25.490 --> 00:24:26.880
<i>Please look forward to it!</i>

